Before writing any code for a feature, do this first and show it to me:

1. USER GOAL
   Who is using this (owner, service advisor, mechanic, accountant) and what are they trying to finish, in one sentence.

2. FLOW MAP
   List the screens in order, for example: List -> Create -> Detail -> Edit -> Status change -> Done.
   For each step, state:
   - what the user sees
   - the single primary action
   - where that action takes them next
   - what happens on success, on error, and when there is no data

3. ENTRY AND EXIT POINTS
   Where the user arrives from (sidebar, customer page, vehicle page) and where they land after finishing. No dead ends: every screen must have a clear next step or a way back.

Wait for my confirmation of the flow map before building.

UI RULES
- English action buttons, nav labels, page titles and modal titles use Title Case (`Add Bay`, `Add Vendor`) — see `ui-labels.mdc`. Never `Add bay`.
- Use shadcn/ui components only for UI primitives (Button, Card, Table, Dialog, Sheet, Form, Input, Select, Tabs, Badge, DropdownMenu, Toast, Skeleton, Alert, Breadcrumb). Add missing ones with the shadcn CLI instead of hand-writing them.
- Every page has: a title, a one-line description, a breadcrumb, and exactly one primary button.
- List pages: search, filters, a table with a status Badge, row actions in a DropdownMenu, pagination, and an empty state with a button to create the first record.
- Create and edit use a full page for long forms and a Sheet or Dialog for short ones. Use react-hook-form + zod with inline field errors.
- Detail pages show a summary header (key info + status + primary action), then Tabs for related data (e.g. vehicle -> service history, invoices).
- Status changes (e.g. service order: Received -> In Progress -> Ready -> Delivered) use a visible status Badge and a single "next step" button, not a dropdown of every status. Destructive actions require a confirm dialog.
- Every async action has: loading state on the button, success toast, error toast with a plain-language message.
- Every list and detail page has a loading Skeleton and an empty state.
- Labels use garage language (Job Card, Estimate, Delivered), not database terms. All text goes through next-intl (en, hi, gu).
- Mobile first: mechanics use phones in the workshop. Tables become cards on small screens, tap targets at least 44px.
- Consistent layout: same page header, same spacing, same card style on every page. Reuse existing components before creating new ones.

AFTER BUILDING
- Walk through the flow once as the user and list any step where the user would not know what to do next, then fix it.
- Confirm every item in the prompt was implemented. List anything skipped.
- No code comments. Give full file contents for changed files.
